author ai
group cli
note The cli crate: the command-line boundary both front ends drive. Its surface is small: Invocation::parse turns arguments into a checked command, exec runs it against an Index and a Map and writes its report to an Output, and every failure comes back as a Failure value, never as text. All wording lives in wire.rs (the clap types, every output line, every error message); convert.rs turns clap's plain strings and numbers into domain values; exec.rs does the work through Map and Index methods. The crate never prints and never saves: the binary decides where an Output goes (Channel) and whether to save, the GUI shows it in its console. What it guarantees: the CLI and the GUI's command line accept the same commands, with the same help and the same errors, because both go through this one parse and exec.

